91740:The D.110c-0b candidate decision is:
91744:| Stable genesis/root authority signs the current checkpoint  | Directly authenticates a current anchor under the creator key committed by a separately pin-verified genesis anchor carrier. Supports evolving ACL/state/history fields while the `creator-trusted-v1` signer remains invariant; does not solve future seal-key rotation. | O(1) existing-v1 current-record bytes, one fixed caller-held genesis invite carrier, and fixed rollback generations, plus the existing RFC 9162 accumulator's absolute safe-integer ceiling of at most 53 peaks; existing Ed25519 plus anchor/QC/history checks. | Browser-feasible with existing primitives, record schema, and no new crypto dependency or wire field. It still requires a new reviewed protocol-v3 checkpoint opener, closure-law contract, durable compatibility transition, and authenticated freshness floor. | Untrusted genesis-carrier/current-record bytes are fully reverified and cross-bound. A caller-held authenticated expected head/floor is required to reject a valid stale checkpoint; a new client with only genesis cannot infer latestness. The bounded immediate-predecessor rollback closure supplies the genuine epoch-N-1 trust needed to verify the retained N-1→N QC. Archive bytes grow separately. Prune only after authentic durable replacement, head installation, snapshot/availability/outbox gates, and two rollback generations. **Selected for creator-only integrity/control compaction, conditional on D.110c-0b0 selecting a real freshness-floor owner.** |
